# Model Selection (Usage Savings Priority)

**Default:** Composer 2.5. **Escalate:** GPT 5.6 Terra when Composer would defer, loop, or need multiple turns.

Owner priority is **quota efficiency**, not “always use the bigger model.” Pick the model that finishes the job in the **fewest correct turns**.

## Decision rule (apply first)

```
Can Composer 2.5 finish in ONE approved turn — one file, ≤30 lines, no Master Bible?
  → Composer 2.5

Otherwise
  → GPT 5.6 Terra (first message must include a tight numbered plan)
```

Composer 2.5 workflow limits live in `AGENTS.md` § Composer 2.5. This rule only governs **which model to open the chat with**.

## Use Composer 2.5

| Task | Why it saves usage |
|------|-------------------|
| Read-only Q&A, grep, “how does X work?” | One cheap turn, no edit risk |
| Code review, audit, diff explanation | No implementation churn |
| Tiny fix (≤5 lines, one file, no new logic) | Designed scope |
| Small-medium fix (~6–30 lines, one file) with clear approved plan | Surgical edit, no rewrite |
| `.tres` / enum / constant tweak | Data-only |
| Apply exact doc/rule diff owner already wrote | No exploration |

## Use GPT 5.6 Terra

| Situation | Why Terra can cost less overall |
|-----------|----------------------------------|
| `class_abilities.txt` / Master Bible (skills, passives, keywords, promotions) | Composer 2.5 defers — bouncing models wastes turns |
| Multi-file change (2+ files) | One Terra turn vs many Composer propose/approve cycles |
| Medium edit (~30–100 lines) or whole function/system | Composer caps at small-medium |
| Architecture, new subsystem, sim resolution order | Partial Composer attempts cost more than one correct pass |
| Determinism / timeline / co-op / preview==commit bugs | Needs depth; failed micro-patches are expensive |
| Owner already knows the fix but scope spans files | Terra + numbered plan avoids exploratory loops |
| Phase milestone or “implement Phase N” | Beyond Composer scope |

**Terra first message must include:** numbered steps, files/functions, acceptance criteria. No wandering.

## Honor & Iron quick map

| Work | Model |
|------|--------|
| Explain existing code | Composer 2.5 |
| Null check, signal, typo, one-file micro-fix | Composer 2.5 |
| Read-only phase audit | Composer 2.5 |
| Class / skill from Master Bible | GPT 5.6 Terra |
| Multi-file combat, preview, or commit pipeline | GPT 5.6 Terra |
| Living sandbox slice (shader + scene + toggle) | GPT 5.6 Terra |

## Usage traps (both models)

1. **Composer proposal loops** — each follow-up “also fix…” is a new gate. Bundle scope or switch to Terra once past small-medium.
2. **Subagents** — burn quota twice (`AGENTS.md`); avoid unless owner explicitly requests.
3. **Terra without a plan** — one expensive wandering turn costs more than Composer read-only + Terra implement.
4. **Wrong model for Bible work** — Composer defers; owner pays defer message + Terra anyway.
5. **Fast mode** — never for Composer 2.5 (`AGENTS.md`).

## Agent behavior

- At chat start or when scope grows mid-chat, **state which model fits** and why (one sentence).
- If Composer 2.5 and task is Terra-tier → **stop and recommend Terra** with the decision rule; do not attempt medium+ work.
- If Terra-tier work is assigned to Composer 2.5 → recommend switching before editing.
